llvm-3.7.1 local rule: an atomic read-modify-write of 32 bits or less ends
a common tail in BranchFolding, and a block holding one is not
tail-duplicated
(no upstream state)

Adopted (docs/DECISIONS.md D96, round 585D): moved from tools/patches/proposed/
into tools/patches/, the fourteenth of the line's seventeen in the glob's order
(after structor-01, before tlsprot-01). The shared install under tools/cc is
rebuilt with it in a round of its own; until then the installed compiler does
not hold it.

This patch CHANGES BRANCHFOLDING'S TAIL MERGE AND TAILDUPLICATION ONLY. Two
changes, nothing else:
  BranchFolding.cpp, ComputeCommonTailLength (:319-365): the comparison
    stops at an instruction that loads and stores through a volatile memory
    operand of at most 4 bytes, as it stops at inline asm (the FIXME at
    :354-360). SelectionDAG marks every atomic's memory operand volatile
    (SelectionDAG::getAtomic), so on x86 these are `lock` xadd, cmpxchg,
    inc, dec, add, sub, or and and of a dword (or narrower). Instructions
    after it in the tail still merge (0x52d3e0: the test and branch after
    two releases are one block).
  TailDuplication.cpp, shouldTailDuplicate (:551-605): a block holding such
    an instruction is not duplicated (both runs, early and late).
Unchanged: every other instruction, the tail-merge size (3) and the
fall-through and adjacent-block rules (:567-581), a qword atomic (merged as
in 3.7.1), JumpThreading's own rule (jumpthread-01) and SimplifyCFG. No
other patch of the list touches these two files; it applies to the 3.7.1
tarball's and after the others in any order.

Question (rounds 372B, 569D, 576D, 579D): the base keeps two identical
atomic read-modify-writes apart before one successor where 3.7.1 merges
them: 0x857df0's two reader-count drops (`lock dec dword ptr [r15]`, one
falling into the loop's test, one jumping to it), 0x52d3e0's and 0xd8feb0's
two Name releases (`lock xadd dword`, result read by the shared `test eax,
eax`), while it merges a whole arm holding a `lock xadd qword` whose result
is read (0xccadb0, ~Object016b9280: the arms of `test al, 0x10` merged, the
test left with no branch at 0xccaeb2).

Evidence (scratch d579/). The installed tree's BranchFolding.cpp and
TailDuplication.cpp (equal to the 3.7.1 tarball's) with switches, linked
ahead of the installed build's archives (control: switches off, the whole
game module byte-identical to the build's, 0 symbols differ), and the
patch's own two files built the same way (byte-identical to the switch
build over the whole module).
  Base census, game region (tails3.py): 675 pairs of predecessors of one
    block whose common tail holds a lock instruction, in 127 functions, ALL
    dword: xadd 199, cmpxchg 395, dec 70, inc 11 (481 that 3.7.1's own
    profitability rules would merge: a fall-through predecessor, or a tail
    of 2 or more with both branches stripped); 0 qword pairs (qword lock instructions in the
    region: cmpxchg 3329, xadd 869, inc 362, dec 4). Merged sites read from
    a flag test left without its branch: 0xccadb0 and 0xbb7bc0, both
    `lock xadd qword` releases of a 64-bit count; no dword one.
  Module census (-tail-merge-log): 3.7.1 merges 12 tails holding an atomic
    in the game module; one is a matched row (~Object016b9280, LXADD64,
    the base's merge); the other eleven are drafts: ten merge a dword one
    (LOCK_DEC32m, LOCK_INC32m, LXADD32) or a plain volatile DEC32m, and one
    an LCMPXCHG64 (Object016b4ce0::find, FUN_01390e90: its compare-exchange
    loop is one block in the base, as 3.7.1 and the rule give).
  The rule over the whole module: 10 symbols change, 0 matched rows change
    (0 rows lost); 7 drafts equal: FUN_0046f770, FUN_0046f980,
    FUN_004ba970, FUN_0052d3e0, FUN_00857df0, FUN_00857f80, FUN_00d8feb0.
    Lower by score only, each explained by the base's bytes: FUN_002e1b30
    (now the base's four `lock inc` and two `lock xadd`, 3.7.1 gave three
    incs; its registers differ), FUN_00e5c690 (the draft's volatile counter
    decrement, a plain `dec dword ptr`, has no counterpart in the base),
    FUN_00e70cc0 (the draft holds a Name release after its call that the
    base does not have; 3.7.1 merged its two copies).
  The merge rule alone: 3 drafts equal (0x4ba970, 0x52d3e0, 0xd8feb0);
    0x857df0's class stays at 0.64 (the pre-RA TailDuplicate copies the
    second find's one-instruction drop block into its two exits). The
    duplication rule's width cannot be told by the module (any atomic, or
    only one whose result is unused, gives the same objects); it takes the
    merge rule's.

Rules the bytes exclude: an atomic ends a tail whatever its width (round
576D v2/v3: loses 0xccadb0); only an atomic whose result is unused (v5:
0x52d3e0 and 0xd8feb0 stay merged, their xadd's result is read); only as
the tail's last instruction (0x3fd0a0 keeps {lock dec; mov dword store; jmp}
apart, and 61 cmpxchg pairs keep {cmpxchg; pushfq; pop} apart); unless the
tail holds a conditional branch (at BranchFolding 0x52d3e0's and 0x857df0's
tails are {atomic; test; jcc}, three or more with the branch, and the base
keeps them apart; measured with the duplication rule, this rule and the
last-only one each make only FUN_004ba970 equal); the pseudo's kind
(LOCK_DEC against LXADD: 0x52d3e0's LXADD32 apart, 0xccadb0's LXADD64
merged); a stop at any volatile memory
operand (round 576D v1: 9 rows lost); whole blocks only (0x857df0's two
drop blocks are whole).

Source forms the bytes exclude: the base's two drops are one machine
instruction (`lock dec dword ptr [r15]`, both through the call's kept
address), and MachineInstr::isIdenticalTo compares only opcode and
operands (MachineInstr.cpp:211-219), so any source that gives the base's
bytes gives two identical instructions at BranchFolding, and a
one-instruction tail with a fall-through predecessor is merged (:567-573)
or made one by OptimizeBlock's move of a jmp-ended block before its
successor (:1508-1524). Compiled (round 569D): the loop rotated (u85),
unrotated (v85) and with the test last (w85): each merged; the `while`
form gives one find (300 bytes against the base's two). A source that
differs at the instruction (a folded drop for one find) gives a byte the
base does not have.

NO upstream state. No release of BranchFolding or TailDuplication from 3.3
to 4.0.0 stops at an atomic or a memory width. Sony authorship of this is
not shown; the width is what the sites separate, not a mechanism: the only
merged atomic sites are one 64-bit count (SharedRef00901550's, volatile in
the tree's source, the dword counts are not).

Refuted by: one base site where two identical dword atomic
read-modify-writes are merged by a tail merge (a dword lock instruction in
a block that a flag test left without its branch, or a draft whose
3.7.1-merged dword atomic is one block in the base with no other
difference), or one where two identical qword ones are kept apart before
one successor.

--- a/lib/CodeGen/BranchFolding.cpp
+++ b/lib/CodeGen/BranchFolding.cpp
@@ -313,6 +313,21 @@
   return HashMachineInstr(I);
 }
 
+/// Local rule (tailmerge-01): an atomic read-modify-write of 32 bits or less
+/// ends a common tail, as inline asm does. SelectionDAG marks the memory
+/// operand of every atomic volatile (SelectionDAG::getAtomic), so the test is
+/// an instruction that loads and stores through a volatile memory operand of
+/// at most 4 bytes.
+static bool isNarrowAtomicRMW(const MachineInstr *MI) {
+  if (!MI->mayLoad() || !MI->mayStore())
+    return false;
+  for (MachineInstr::mmo_iterator I = MI->memoperands_begin(),
+       E = MI->memoperands_end(); I != E; ++I)
+    if ((*I)->isVolatile() && (*I)->getSize() <= 4)
+      return true;
+  return false;
+}
+
 /// ComputeCommonTailLength - Given two machine basic blocks, compute the number
 /// of instructions they actually have in common together at their end.  Return
 /// iterators for the first shared instruction in each block.
@@ -357,7 +372,9 @@
         // relative order. This is untenable because normal compiler
         // optimizations (like this one) may reorder and/or merge these
         // directives.
-        I1->isInlineAsm()) {
+        I1->isInlineAsm() ||
+        // Local rule (tailmerge-01).
+        isNarrowAtomicRMW(I1)) {
       ++I1; ++I2;
       break;
     }
--- a/lib/CodeGen/TailDuplication.cpp
+++ b/lib/CodeGen/TailDuplication.cpp
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include "llvm/CodeGen/MachineBranchProbabilityInfo.h"
 #include "llvm/CodeGen/MachineFunctionPass.h"
 #include "llvm/CodeGen/MachineInstrBuilder.h"
+#include "llvm/CodeGen/MachineMemOperand.h"
 #include "llvm/CodeGen/MachineModuleInfo.h"
 #include "llvm/CodeGen/MachineRegisterInfo.h"
 #include "llvm/CodeGen/MachineSSAUpdater.h"
@@ -589,6 +590,15 @@
     if (I->isNotDuplicable())
       return false;
 
+    // Local rule (tailmerge-01): a block holding an atomic read-modify-write
+    // of 32 bits or less (a load and store through a volatile memory operand
+    // of at most 4 bytes) is not duplicated.
+    if (I->mayLoad() && I->mayStore())
+      for (MachineInstr::mmo_iterator M = I->memoperands_begin(),
+           ME = I->memoperands_end(); M != ME; ++M)
+        if ((*M)->isVolatile() && (*M)->getSize() <= 4)
+          return false;
+
     // Do not duplicate 'return' instructions if this is a pre-regalloc run.
     // A return may expand into a lot more instructions (e.g. reload of callee
     // saved registers) after PEI.
